# /sdd-clear

Purpose:
  Clear all SDD working context and start fresh for the next task —
  delegating the final context wipe to the AI agent's NATIVE /clear.

Owns: commands/sdd-clear.sdd

Description:
  Clear all context and start fresh for next task. Use when transitioning
  between distinct tasks to prevent context pollution. Delegates to the
  host agent's native clear command.

Usage:
  /sdd-clear
  /sdd-clear --save-state
  /sdd-clear --archive

Options:
  --save-state  Persist current task state before clearing
  --archive     Archive context to history before clearing

Mode: READ_ONLY (delegates wipe to native)

InitialLoad:
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing)
  - .sdd/projects/sddra/context/active.sdd

Output:
  [tokens: cleared]
  [state: fresh]
  [history: archived|discarded]
  [native: /clear delegated]

Rules:
  [CLEAR-01] /sdd-clear MUST NOT reimplement context wipe — delegate to native /clear.
  [CLEAR-02] /sdd-clear MUST persist SDD state if requested.
  [CLEAR-03] /sdd-clear MUST log the clear operation to history if archived.

Navigation:
  ChainGraph: @../chains/graph.sdd
  Runtime: @../runtime/state.sdd
  History: @../history/INDEX.sdd

State: +
